+# Cache Eviction Policy
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use LRU (Least Recently Used) eviction with a 300-second TTL, chosen for better temporal locality; this supersedes an earlier decision to use LFU (Least Frequently Used) eviction, and the fixed TTL ensures entries expire automatically, preventing stale data and reducing memory bloat from long-lived cache entries.
